# Closed decisions that must SURVIVE an edit: REJECTED, or DEFERRED under a
# stated trigger. Baseline for `microlith check --records .spec-records SPEC.md`.
#
# These live here and not in §R because §R is RESEARCH (external findings with
# sources, FORMAT 4.1.0). A closed OPTION is a claim about a decision over
# time, which no single text can answer -- so the checker owns the rule and
# this repo owns the list.
#
# WHY THESE ARE THE FRAGILE ONES: none describes anything bbx builds. To a
# compaction pass counting bytes they read as the most deletable text in the
# file. Delete them and every gate stays green -- and then someone re-proposes
# a crate-per-verb workspace and nothing says it was already answered, with a
# measurement.

C1  crate-per-verb workspace REJECTED
C2  own tokenizer / own bytes-4 REJECTED
C3  own §-parser, fmt, id checker REJECTED
C4  name-encoded grouping REJECTED
C5  dir federation as the ONLY axis DEFERRED
C6  single-glob workspace DEFERRED
C7  ceiling counting whole `.rs` file REJECTED
C8  `default.rs` REJECTED
C9  grep-enforced dep facade REJECTED
C10 `default.nix` laziness as a model DEFERRED
